      "problem": "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4-\\lambda  \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )((4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(20-4\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-16)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4-4) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
